<title>MEXICO: Geo joins Salfa in Chilean housing deal.</title>
<headline>Geo joins Salfa in Chilean housing deal.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Corporacion Geo, a developer of low-income housing, said it has joined Chile's Constructora Salfa in a 50-50 partnership, Geosal SA, to develop affordable housing in Chile.</p>
<p>The aim is to build and sell more than 3,000 homes annually, priced between $20,000 and $25,000, over the next three years, representing 15 percent of GEO's consolidated sales in 2000, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The partners will initially provide Geosal with $12 million in equity, with both debt and equity used to finance the projects.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City Newsroom 525 728-9560))</p>
